---
epr-meta-version: 1
id: capability-package-governance
purpose: >
  Governs the elohim-native capability package tree — the JSON packages under
  `agents/` and `skills/` that are the canonical source for generated Claude/Codex runtime
  surfaces (`.claude/{agents,skills}/*`, `.codex/{agents,skills}/*`; see
  `.claude/skills/elohim-package-authoring/SKILL.md`). Binds the `capability-governance` policy
  (observation tier — never blocks) so editing a package surfaces the re-import discipline: run
  `package-projections.mjs verify` (and regenerate when intended) before the runtime projections
  are trusted again.
rules:
  - id: capability-package-governance
    policy: capability-governance@1
---

# `.epr-meta/elohim/packages` — capability package governance

Binds `capability-governance@1` from the policy registry (`.claude/epr-meta/policies.yaml`):
`*.json` writes under this tree are measured against a soft/hard LoC ceiling (observation tier —
never blocks). The policy's `why` names the real discipline this tree lives by: a package here is
the source of truth, `.claude/*` and `.codex/*` are its generated projections — after editing a
package, run:

```
node elohim/sdk/domains/elohim-agent/scripts/package-projections.mjs verify
```

and regenerate with `--write-fixtures --write-runtime` when the projections should move. Never
hand-edit the generated `.claude/`/`.codex/` surfaces directly.
